
#### Build & Installation Guide

**1. Set Kernel Path
Edit `Makefile` before compiling:
KERNEL_DIR ?= /path/to/your/linux-kernel  # MUST match development board's kernel!

**2. Compile Drive
make

**3. Load/Unload Driver
# Install TNPU driver with 16MB continuous memory
insmod tnpu.ko cma_pool_size=0x1000000
# Set clock (600MHz)
insmod tnpu.ko parent_clk_name=apll tnpu_clk_rate=600000000 cma_pool_size=0x1000000
# Uninstall
rmmod tnpu

Generally, driver installation failures are caused by kernel mismatch:
> $(KERNEL_DIR) MUST match the kernel running on your dev board.
> Verify vermagic with 'uname -r' on board and 'modinfo tnpu.ko' on host.

#### Debugging Options
Enable in 'tnpu_drv.h':
#define CONFIG_TNPU_DEV_DEBUG        // Driver init/shutdown
#define CONFIG_TNPU_MEM_DEBUG        // CMA memory allocations
#define CONFIG_TNPU_CORE_DEBUG       // Library loading & scheduling
#define CONFIG_TNPU_DUTY_RATIO_DEBUG // Performance monitoring

